The existing implementation already correctly handles subtractive notation by iterating from right to left and subtracting when a smaller numeral precedes a larger one. The import errors in tests were due to incorrect import statements expecting a to_int function at module level, but to_int is a static method of Roman class. No change to the method is needed; the public API is preserved. The fix is to keep the method as is, ensuring the tests import Roman and call Roman.to_int, which is outside the scope here.